From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wintypes, windows.applicationmodel: ValueSet, PropertySet, ResourceContext

Windows Terminal hands each new tab's connection its settings in a ValueSet; ValueSet is registered to wintypes, which made no object for it (E_NOTIMPL), and the tab failed. wintypes now hands ValueSet and PropertySet (newly registered) to windows.applicationmodel, whose property set (CoreApplication.Properties') makes them: a string-keyed map of objects, observable and iterable. Windows Terminal also asks for ResourceContext.GetForViewIndependentUse, a class that only existed as the resource manager's default context: ResourceContext is now activatable, with its statics (CreateMatchingContext, GetForCurrentView, GetForViewIndependentUse, the global qualifier values, GetForUIContext) and Clone/Reset on its contexts.
---
diff --git a/dlls/windows.applicationmodel/main.c b/dlls/windows.applicationmodel/main.c
index acd20b6..72dbcef 100644
--- a/dlls/windows.applicationmodel/main.c
+++ b/dlls/windows.applicationmodel/main.c
@@ -76,6 +76,13 @@ HRESULT WINAPI DllGetActivationFactory( HSTRING classid, IActivationFactory **fa
     if (!wcscmp( buffer, RuntimeClass_Windows_ApplicationModel_LimitedAccessFeatures ))
         IActivationFactory_QueryInterface( limited_access_factory, &IID_IActivationFactory, (void **)factory );
 
+    if (!wcscmp( buffer, L"Windows.Foundation.Collections.ValueSet" ) ||
+        !wcscmp( buffer, L"Windows.Foundation.Collections.PropertySet" ))
+        IActivationFactory_QueryInterface( property_set_factory, &IID_IActivationFactory, (void **)factory );
+
+    if (!wcscmp( buffer, L"Windows.ApplicationModel.Resources.Core.ResourceContext" ))
+        IActivationFactory_QueryInterface( resource_context_factory, &IID_IActivationFactory, (void **)factory );
+
     if (!wcscmp( buffer, L"Windows.ApplicationModel.Resources.Core.ResourceManager" ))
         IActivationFactory_QueryInterface( resource_manager_factory, &IID_IActivationFactory, (void **)factory );
 
